  "_commit": {
    "id": "8b91a688644e71eafdf979ebecb214d7ad1e9c86",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "fix: preserve a matrix label's true extent past an all-zero trailing row/column (0.99.26)\n\nwriteParquet,ANY only attaches index->label categories (the metadata a\nreader uses to recover the true axis size) when the array already has\ndimnames at the point it captures them, before it assigns synthetic\nseq_len() dimnames for the physical write. A spatialLabels() matrix is\nnormally dimname-less, so no categories were ever recorded for the\nspatial_label_coord path added above, and .readParquetArray() fell back\nto inferring the shape from the sparse COO data alone -- undercounting\nwhenever the dropped (all-zero) entries included a whole trailing row or\ncolumn.\n\nFixed by synthesizing dimnames on the label matrix (the same seq_len()\nvalues ANY would assign internally anyway) before writing it, so\ncategories are always attached regardless of what the input happened to\nhave. Added a regression test using a label whose only nonzero entry is\nat row 1/col 1; the existing round-trip test has a nonzero in both the\nlast row and last column, which masked this gap.\n",
    "time": 1792097605
  },
